{"name":"Sixteen Million Pink","hex":"#fd02ff","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sixteen","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Numeral","definitions":["The cardinal number occurring after fifteen and before seventeen, represented in Arabic numerals as 16 and in Roman numerals as XVI."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sixteen"},{"term":"million","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Numeral","definitions":["The cardinal number 1 000 000: 10; a thousand thousand (1,000).","An unspecified very large number."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/million"},{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sixteen (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Sixteen is the fifth studio album by American singer Stacy Lattisaw. Released on July 11, 1983, by Cotillion Records, Lattisaw was 16 years old at the time of this release. The single, \"Miracles\", peaked at number thirteen on the U.S. R&B chart in 1983."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/43/Stacy_Lattisaw_Sixteen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sixteen_(album)","wikidata":"Q7533035"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wik